{"version":"0.12.19","prev_tag":"v0.12.18","target":"default","tag_prefix":"","area_scope":[],"commits":[{"sha":"aef8c0c98a975a9bd3ceafc6bcedc3e2da37e408","title":"sessions: preserve live terminals and add shell command blocks (#1269)","files":[".gitignore",".lf/directions/macos-terminal.md","README.md","TESTING.md","docs/lf.md","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/util.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/human_session.rs","rust/loopflow/src/run_record.rs","scripts/loopflow-dev.py","swift/GhosttyKitPatches/0001-command-blocks.patch","swift/GhosttyKitPatches/README.md","swift/Loopflow/Models/MultiplexerStore.swift","swift/LoopflowMac/GhosttyResources/REVISION","swift/LoopflowMac/GhosttyResources/share/ghostty/shell-integration/bash/bash-preexec.sh","swift/LoopflowMac/GhosttyResources/share/ghostty/shell-integration/bash/ghostty.bash","swift/LoopflowMac/GhosttyResources/share/ghostty/shell-integration/elvish/lib/ghostty-integration.elv","swift/LoopflowMac/GhosttyResources/share/ghostty/shell-integration/fish/vendor_conf.d/ghostty-shell-integration.fish","swift/LoopflowMac/GhosttyResources/share/ghostty/shell-integration/nushell/vendor/autoload/ghostty.nu","swift/LoopflowMac/GhosttyResources/share/ghostty/shell-integration/zsh/.zshenv","swift/LoopflowMac/GhosttyResources/share/ghostty/shell-integration/zsh/ghostty-integration","swift/LoopflowMac/GhosttyResources/share/terminfo/67/ghostty","swift/LoopflowMac/GhosttyResources/share/terminfo/78/xterm-ghostty","swift/LoopflowMac/GhosttyResources/share/terminfo/ghostty.terminfo","swift/LoopflowMac/Services/Ghostty/GhosttyManager.swift","swift/LoopflowMac/Services/Ghostty/GhosttyTerminalView.swift","swift/LoopflowMac/Views/PodiumView.swift","swift/LoopflowMac/Views/SessionsView.swift","swift/LoopflowMac/Views/TaskWorkspaceView.swift","swift/LoopflowTests/GhosttyTerminalInputTests.swift","swift/LoopflowTests/MultiplexerStoreTests.swift","swift/LoopflowTests/SessionsPolishTests.swift","swift/LoopflowTests/SessionsStoreTests.swift","swift/LoopflowUITests/SessionsInteractionTests.swift","swift/Package.swift","swift/README.md","swift/project.yml","wave/product/MEMORY.md"]}],"merged_prs":[{"number":1269,"title":"sessions: preserve live terminals and add shell command blocks","body":"## Evaluate\n\nRun on macOS:\n\n```bash\nswift test --package-path swift --filter 'GhosttyTerminalInputTests|SessionsStoreTests|SessionsPolishTests|MultiplexerStoreTests'\nuv run python scripts/test.py --loopflow\ncargo test -p loopflow lf::commands::util::tests\n```\n\nThe focused tests exercise explicit takeover, retained workspaces, window-local surface ownership, paste routing through split panes into live PTYs, and command-block copying to the pasteboard. Rust tests distinguish an intentional move from an unexplained SIGTERM. The Xcode suite also checks the terminal fallback configuration. These commands are evaluation steps, not results from this review.\n\nIn the Ghostty-enabled app:\n\n- Close and reopen a Session pane, then navigate between Sessions and Work or switch repositories. The terminal should retain its running client and contents.\n- Select a Session active elsewhere. Its client should continue until **Move here**; the old terminal should then report that the Session moved.\n- In an integrated shell, run a command with output, click its completed block, and press Command-C. The clipboard should contain the command and output; the live prompt should remain editable.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nNavigating the app or closing a Session pane should preserve ongoing work. Explicit takeover makes stopping another terminal a deliberate action, while accurate terminal status and focused paste routing prevent confusing or misplaced input. Shell command blocks make completed commands and their output easy to copy together.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Retain pane layouts and live surfaces per repository within each window, with distinct Session, shell, and Task terminal identities. Show VIEWING, RUNNING, and ELSEWHERE states and recover from provider exits.\n- Defer replacement until the prepared launch executes. Record move/completion intent so deliberate provider termination exits cleanly while unexplained failures remain errors.\n- Add shell command-block selection, highlighting, and copying through a patched Ghostty C API. Bundle matching shell integration and terminfo, pin the versioned framework and checksum, and provide a rebuild command.\n- Restrict terminal shortcuts to the focused pane and add clipboard, image, and file-drop handling. Opening a Session beside a focused shell preserves that shell.\n\n## Risks / Not included\n\n- **Move here** loses unsent text in the previous client; the UI explains this before takeover.\n- Retention lasts within the window’s lifetime. Closing a shell pane still ends its shell.\n- Command blocks require supported shell integration and apply only to shell panes. The pinned build excludes automatic integration for macOS `/bin/bash`.","files":[],"additions":4554,"deletions":367,"changed_files":37,"merge_commit":"aef8c0c98a975a9bd3ceafc6bcedc3e2da37e408"}],"decisions":null,"previous_release_notes":"# v0.12.18\n\n<!-- loopflow:release-notes=narrative;gate=safe -->\n\nv0.12.18 makes chapter changes easier to assess and safer to reset. New chapter workflows review KR evidence across repository, project, and Wave scopes, while interactive starts preserve human direction through scoped Runs and apply only the accepted plan. Terminal skill catalogs also stay aligned without changing redirected output.\n\n## Review and reset plans as chapters\n\nChapter work now has built-in start and review paths at repository, project, and Wave scope. Reviews can judge KR progress autonomously; starts capture human direction before scoped Runs, reconcile the resulting challenges, and carry the accepted plan forward.\n\n- Six built-in chapter skills cover starting and reviewing work at all three scopes.\n- Repository chapter starts record human Wave direction before launching scoped Runs.\n- Interactive starts reconcile the Runs' challenges and apply only the plan the human accepts.\n- Bound and nested Runs leave their edits uncommitted for the owning Task to inspect and checkpoint.\n\n## Small changes\n\n- `lf list` now returns to column zero on each terminal newline, preventing skill catalog output from drifting right in raw terminals.\n- Redirected and captured `lf list` output keeps its original LF bytes.","source_limits":{"context_bytes":131072,"commits":256,"merged_prs":200,"files_per_change":100,"area_scopes":32,"name_bytes":256,"title_bytes":300,"path_bytes":512,"pr_body_bytes":4096,"decisions_bytes":16384,"previous_release_notes_bytes":16384,"release_notes_bytes":61440},"omissions":{"commits":0,"merged_prs":0,"commit_files":0,"pr_files":0,"area_scopes":0,"text_bytes":0,"decisions_bytes":0,"previous_release_notes_bytes":0}}